<section class="intro"><article class="card"><h2>Why Eureka Springs is an Ozark heavyweight</h2><p>Eureka Springs traces its modern founding to 1879, and the entire town was placed on the National Register of Historic Places in 1970. Today the destination blends historic architecture and springs with art, dining, nightlife and outdoor recreation.</p><p>The destination's visitor resources highlight outdoor recreation, eclectic accommodations, food and a year-round calendar. Around town, visitors can connect with Lake Leatherwood, the Kings River, Beaver Lake, trails, caves and distinctive attractions.</p><div class="actions"><a class="btn primary" href="/guides/best-things-to-do-eureka-springs">Top things to do →</a><a class="btn ghost" style="background:#f0ede4;color:#193b29;border:0" href="/guides/cabins-near-eureka-springs">Eureka Springs cabins</a></div></article><aside class="card stats"><div class="stat"><b>66+</b><span>springs in and around Eureka Springs</span></div><div class="stat"><b>1,600 ac</b><span>Lake Leatherwood City Park</span></div><div class="stat"><b>25+ mi</b><span>hiking and biking trails at Lake Leatherwood</span></div></aside></section>
